From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AlmarionAI <150292831+AlmarionAI@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 21:45:34 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] [budget] tighten-only agent budgets: row cap and
 pre-execution cost gate

Add GUC_RATCHET: a PGC_SUSET variable with this flag may still be set from
the session by a role without SET privilege on it, but only to a tighter
limit (0 means no limit), including via RESET, set_config() and function
SET clauses. A frontend that is not a superuser can therefore lower an
agent's budget per transaction, and the agent cannot raise it again.

agent_max_cost refuses, in standard_ExecutorStart, any plan whose estimated
total cost exceeds the budget, before it does any work. It applies at every
nesting level, so SQL run through query_to_xml() and the like is gated, and
under EXPLAIN ANALYZE; EXPLAIN without ANALYZE is allowed.

agent_max_rows caps the rows a SELECT returns to the client (the result
stops at the cap with a NOTICE when more rows exist; queries inside
functions are not capped), and the rows one statement may modify, counted
across all of its ModifyTable nodes so data-modifying CTEs count too; such
a statement fails as a whole. Regression test agent_budget.
